บ A LOVE LETTER TO THE DEMOSCENE.                                            บ
บ                                                                            บ
บ What is the demoscene? A computer art subculture that grew out of the      บ
บ cracktros of the 1980s: the animated intros crackers stuck on pirated      บ
บ games to sign their work. Soon people made them for their own sake. A DEMO บ
บ is a program that plays an audiovisual show in real time: no video file,   บ
บ just code, math and music, often squeezed into a few kilobytes and judged  บ
บ at parties by other coders and artists.  (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demoscene) บ
บ                                                                            บ
บ I have always been fascinated by computer generated imagery, and to me the บ
บ demoscene is its highest form: the place where code meets art. A demo is   บ
บ never a recording. It exists for a fraction of a second at a time, in your บ
บ GPU's memory, and then it is gone and drawn again.                         บ
บ                                                                            บ
บ Yes, AI helped to make this: the music, the sprites and much of the code.  บ
บ It is still my love letter to everyone who pioneered this scene, and       บ
บ everyone who keeps it alive. Nothing was cracked here. The only thing that บ
บ got hacked is a perfectly good synthwave sunset.                           บ
บ                                                                            บ
บ -- hodiloves                                                               บ
